          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#general General
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                The power set
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒫
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{P}S
                canonically carries a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partial+order"} partial order
                by containment, making it a
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset"} poset
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                precedes
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
                means that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subset"} subset
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
                (
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ⊆
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \subseteq B
                ).
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cantor%27s+theorem"} Cantor's theorem
                states that there exists no
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/surjection"} surjection
                from
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                to
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒫
                        %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{P}S
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injection"} injection
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi S
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi 𝒫
                        %mi S
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {|S|} \lt {|\mathcal{P}S|}
              %p
                in the usual arithmetic of
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cardinal+numbers"} cardinal numbers
            %li
              %p
                Power sets live in the category
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                of any
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset"} poset
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobjects"} subobjects
                of
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/well-powered+category"} well-powered
                when this poset is
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power+object"} power object
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            %li
              %p
                The power set construction constitutes an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence of categories
                between the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+category"} opposite category
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mo
                        %mi op
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ^{op}
                and that of
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complete+atomic+Boolean+algebras"} complete atomic Boolean algebras
                = succeed "." do
                  %em
                    %a{:href => "Set#OppositeCategory"} Set – Properties – Opposite category and Boolean algebras
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+sets"} finite sets
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence of categories
                between the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+category"} opposite category
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FinSet"} FinSet
                and that of finite
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Boolean+algebras"} Boolean algebras
                = succeed "." do
                  %em
                    %a{:href => "FinSet#OppositeCategory"} FinSet – Opposite category
          %h3#power_set_functor Power set functor
          %p
            The power set construction gives rise to two functors, the contravariant power set functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
